Subject: [PATCH 52/52] Build: optional FFmpeg-free build (/p:FafFfmpeg=false)

Upstream's movie player (6ac2dba0) links FFmpeg 7.1 import libraries and needs
its DLLs beside main.exe, and the build stops without the FFmpeg development
package. /p:FafFfmpeg=false (or FafFfmpeg=false in the environment) builds
without it: FfmpegSfdDecoder.cpp is replaced by FfmpegSfdDecoderDisabled.cpp,
whose Open always throws, so IndependentSfdBackend reports every .sfd movie as
unplayable the way it does a missing file; no FFmpeg library is linked, checked
for or staged. Meant for headless and automated games, which never show a
movie. The default (FafFfmpeg=true) is unchanged.
